#{[17592186518184 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Minkowski distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{p}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{p}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{p}={({\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}{|}^{p})}^{1/p}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{3}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{3} \\\\  & ={‖\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}‖}_{3} \\\\  & ={(|1-2{|}^{3}+|1-(-1){|}^{3}+|-1-(-2){|}^{3})}^{1/3} \\\\  & ={10}^{1/3} \\\\  & ≈2.154.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186518192 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Manhattan distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{1}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{1}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{1}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{1}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{1} \\\\  & ={‖\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}‖}_{1} \\\\  & =|3-4|+|5-(-1)|+|1-6| \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186518194 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Manhattan distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{1}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{1}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{1}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{1}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{1} \\\\  & ={‖\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}‖}_{1} \\\\  & =|1-5|+|-5-1| \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186518198 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Minkowski distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{p}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{p}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{p}={({\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}{|}^{p})}^{1/p}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{5}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{5} \\\\  & ={‖\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}‖}_{5} \\\\  & ={(|3-2{|}^{5}+|1-2{|}^{5})}^{1/5} \\\\  & ={2}^{1/5} \\\\  & ≈1.149.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186518202 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Euclidean distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{2}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}{|}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{2}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{2} \\\\  & ={‖\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}‖}_{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{|-1-2{|}^{2}+|1-3{|}^{2}+|0-1{|}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\  & ≈3.742.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186518208 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Chebyshev distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{\\infty }(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{\\infty }\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{\\infty }=max(|{v}_{1}|,|{v}_{2}|,…,|{v}_{N}|).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{\\infty }(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{\\infty } \\\\  & ={‖\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}‖}_{\\infty } \\\\  & =max(|5-9|,|3-(-9)|) \\\\  & =max(4,12) \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186518219 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Manhattan distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{1}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{1}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{1}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{1}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{1} \\\\  & ={‖\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}‖}_{1} \\\\  & =|7-3|+|4-(-2)| \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186518220 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the Minkowski distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{p}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{p}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{p}={({\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}{|}^{p})}^{1/p}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{6}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{6} \\\\  & ={‖\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}‖}_{6} \\\\  & ={(|2-3{|}^{6}+|-1-0{|}^{6}+|1-2{|}^{6})}^{1/6} \\\\  & ={3}^{1/6} \\\\  & ≈1.201.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186518908 :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-1,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}2 u v^{3}\\\\3 u^{2} + v^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$"] [17592186518908 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}2 v^{3}&6 u v^{2}\\\\6 u&2 v\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(2 v^{3})\\cdot (2 v)-(6 u v^{2})\\cdot (6 u)\\\\& =- 36 u^{2} v^{2} + 4 v^{4}\\\\& =- 4 v^{2} \\left(3 u - v\\right) \\left(3 u + v\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(-1,2)} & =\\left(- 4 v^{2} \\left(3 u - v\\right) \\left(3 u + v\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=-1,v=2}\\\\& =- 4 (2)^{2} \\left(3 (-1) - (2)\\right) \\left(3 (-1) + (2)\\right)\\\\& =-80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|-80|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =80\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186518915 :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-3,-1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}3 u v^{2}\\\\u^{2} + 2 v^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$"] [17592186518915 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}3 v^{2}&6 u v\\\\2 u&4 v\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(3 v^{2})\\cdot (4 v)-(6 u v)\\cdot (2 u)\\\\& =- 12 u^{2} v + 12 v^{3}\\\\& =- 12 v \\left(u - v\\right) \\left(u + v\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(-3,-1)} & =\\left(- 12 v \\left(u - v\\right) \\left(u + v\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=-3,v=-1}\\\\& =- 12 (-1) \\left(- (-1) + (-3)\\right) \\left((-1) + (-3)\\right)\\\\& =96\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|96|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =96\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186518926 :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(1,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2}\\\\\\left(u - v\\right)^{3}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$"] [17592186518926 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}4 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)&8 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)\\\\3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2}&- 3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(4 \\left(u + 2 v\\right))\\cdot (- 3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2})-(8 \\left(u + 2 v\\right))\\cdot (3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2})\\\\& =- 36 u^{3} + 108 u v^{2} - 72 v^{3}\\\\& =- 36 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2} \\left(u + 2 v\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(1,2)} & =\\left(- 36 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2} \\left(u + 2 v\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=1,v=2}\\\\& =- 36 \\left((1) - (2)\\right)^{2} \\left((1) + 2 (2)\\right)\\\\& =-180\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|-180|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =180\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186518930 :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(2,-1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}3 u v^{3}\\\\u^{2} + 2 v^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$"] [17592186518930 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}3 v^{3}&9 u v^{2}\\\\2 u&4 v\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(3 v^{3})\\cdot (4 v)-(9 u v^{2})\\cdot (2 u)\\\\& =- 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 12 v^{4}\\\\& =- 6 v^{2} \\left(3 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(2,-1)} & =\\left(- 6 v^{2} \\left(3 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=2,v=-1}\\\\& =- 6 (-1)^{2} \\left(- 2 (-1)^{2} + 3 (2)^{2}\\right)\\\\& =-60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|-60|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =60\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186518944 :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-1,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}\\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{3}\\\\\\left(u - v\\right)^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$"] [17592186518944 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}3 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2}&6 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2}\\\\2 \\left(u - v\\right)&- 2 \\left(u - v\\right)\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(3 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2})\\cdot (- 2 \\left(u - v\\right))-(6 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2})\\cdot (2 \\left(u - v\\right))\\\\& =- 18 u^{3} - 54 u^{2} v + 72 v^{3}\\\\& =- 18 \\left(u - v\\right) \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2}\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(-1,2)} & =\\left(- 18 \\left(u - v\\right) \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2}\\right)\\big|_{u=-1,v=2}\\\\& =- 18 \\left((-1) - (2)\\right) \\left((-1) + 2 (2)\\right)^{2}\\\\& =486\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|486|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =486\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186518946 :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-2,1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\left(u + v\\right)^{3}\\\\\\left(2 u - v\\right)^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$"] [17592186518946 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\